#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# lommel_s1

#% text
# `lommel_s1(mu, nu, z)` gives the Lommel function `s_(mu, nu)(z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `s_(mu, nu)(z)` is the particular solution of `z^2 w'' + z w' + (z^2 - nu^2) w = z^(mu + 1)` given by the series of DLMF 11.9.3; `mu + nu` and `mu - nu` must not be negative odd integers.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
lommel_s1(0.5, 0.5, 1.0)
#% output
#= 0.4596976941318603

#% cell
lommel_s1(1.5, 0.5, 2.0)
#% output
#= 0.771243185749177

#% cell
lommel_s1(1, 0, 3.0)
#% output
#= 1.2600519549019333

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The differential equation, checked numerically at `z = 1.3` with `mu = 1/2`, `nu = 1/3`:

#% cell
f = z => lommel_s1(0.5, 1/3, z); z0 = 1.3; h = 1.0e-4; z0^2*(f(z0 + h) - 2*f(z0) + f(z0 - h))/h^2 + z0*(f(z0 + h) - f(z0 - h))/(2*h) + (z0^2 - 1/9)*f(z0) - z0^1.5
#% output
#= -3.3976959024073494e-9

